I did not solve this game exactly; I am choosing the uniform distribution, 0.02 on each of the 50 words, as a near-optimal answer.

The reasoning is that any word I favour becomes a cheap first guess for the guesser, so unequal weights tend to help them. Under uniform weights, the best the guesser can do is a first guess that separates all the other words, which gives an expected (1 + 49 × 2) / 50 = 1.98 guesses. If no single guess separates them perfectly, the expectation is slightly higher.

